from pathlib import Path
import re,html,difflib,markdown,json
O=Path(__file__).resolve().parent;R=O.parents[3]
def render(s):return markdown.markdown(re.sub(r'<!--\s*@[^>]*-->','',s),extensions=['extra','sane_lists'])
def image(n,c):return '<figure><a href="'+n+'.png"><img loading="lazy" src="'+n+'.png" alt="'+html.escape(c,quote=True)+'"></a><figcaption>'+c+'</figcaption></figure>'
before=(O/'Color_Pillar.before.md').read_text(encoding='utf-8');after=(R/'commons/maps/Color_Pillar/final.md').read_text(encoding='utf-8');assert after==(O/'Color_Pillar.after.md').read_text(encoding='utf-8')
a=before.split('\n\n');b=after.split('\n\n');pairs=[]
for tag,i,j,k,l in difflib.SequenceMatcher(None,a,b,autojunk=False).get_opcodes():
 if tag=='equal':continue
 pairs.append('<div class="pair"><div><h3>Before</h3>'+(render('\n\n'.join(a[i:j])) or '<p>Added shared illustration.</p>')+'</div><div><h3>Now</h3>'+render('\n\n'.join(b[k:l]))+'</div></div>')
css=re.search(r'<style>(.*?)</style>',(O.parent/'2026-09-23-array-molnar-volume/index.html').read_text(encoding='utf-8'),re.S)[1]
page='<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><title>Pillar — the colour between</title><style>'+css+'</style></head><body><main>'
page+='''<div class="eyebrow">Ada Research · Colour · 23 September 2026</div><h1>The colour between.</h1><p class="intro">The field has a colour there.<br>The collection has no column.</p><p class="status">Applied to <strong>Color_Pillar/final.md</strong>. Three small prose changes and a shared native figure. The existing field, palette wall and secondary artifacts remain.</p><nav><a href="#encounter">Inside the field</a><a href="#collection">Carry a colour</a><a href="#comparison">What changed</a><a href="#reading">Read the chapter</a><a href="#evidence">Evidence</a><a href="/compose/sources?map=Color_Pillar&amp;doc=final">Read and comment</a></nav>'''
page+='<section id="encounter"><h2>A sample rises; a gap lets you through</h2>'+image('field-and-passage','The continuous floor and the thirty-five column materials evaluate the same HSV field. The floor is unshaded; the columns receive light. Equal assigned values need not look identical on these different surfaces.')+'<p>The installation already gives a rule enough room to walk. Along its length saturation increases; across its width hue changes. Between its selected sample positions there is still a colour, and also room for a body to pass.</p><details><summary>The pale edge and a sample address</summary>'+image('pale-edge','A selected standing-height view down the gap between two lines of pillars.')+image('sample-address','The existing label identifies the sample at (1, 0), with its generated hexadecimal colour code.')+'</details></section>'
page+='<section id="collection"><h2>The code travels; the neighbours remain</h2>'+image('named-collections','Twelve authored collections on the existing framed wall. These titles are the project’s interpretations of moods, artists and movements, not claims that each history has one correct palette.')+image('carried-colour','A real swatch from Autumn Melancholy, moved by a supplied grabber through the existing pickup mechanism. Its material and label remain unchanged: #B87333, named Peru by the closest-entry lookup. No tracked hand is shown.')+'<p>The field computes from position. The wall reads authored lists. A carried swatch keeps its recorded value while leaving one company of colours for another. The short list used to choose its colour name is another selection again.</p></section>'
page+='<section id="comparison"><h2>Keep the inquiry close to the walk</h2><p>The prediction prompt becomes a return along the same hue. One sentence gives the gaps a bodily consequence. The swatch paragraph now explains its two kinds of label and follows what moves with it. The opening, coordinate code, dimensions and next-hall question remain.</p>'+''.join(pairs)+'<p><a href="Color_Pillar.diff">Exact manuscript diff</a> · <a href="source-changes.diff">Companion changes</a></p><p>The critical companion now follows the current field, architectural samples and named collections. The complete older gauntlet draft is retained beneath it as historical material, with its unverified claims clearly separated.</p></section>'
page+='<section id="reading"><article class="reading">'+render(after)+'</article></section>'
page+='''<section id="evidence" class="evidence"><h2>What was checked</h2><p>32 focused assertions pass in the isolated production museum: 35 material samples and labels agree with their coordinates; floor UV directions match the field; the lengthwise and crosswise comparisons hold; twelve named wall sets are present. A real swatch follows the production pickup mechanism through supplied movement, retains its material/name, releases and is restored to its original placement.</p><p>Supplied key input drives the ordinary museum controller along a gap between columns, across a gap between rows and back toward the pale edge. The body remains on the supporting floor. This checks three selected paths, not every possible route.</p><p>The first palette-wall camera looked through a pillar. The final run moves only that camera closer to the wall. Native and composed views were inspected. The shared figure combines an elevated view and the reached body position plus a 1.65-metre eye offset; no synthetic image represents the museum.</p><p>No production source, map, geometry, control or primary selection changed. No tracked-controller reach, headset comfort, colour-calibration, learner or performance claim; no live restart, live bake/save overwrite, commit or frozen book/audio rebuild.</p><p><a href="report.json">Runtime record</a> · <a href="source_manifest.json">Capture inputs</a> · <a href="verification.json">Preservation and publication checks</a> · <a href="SUMMARY.md">Findings and decisions</a></p></section><footer>Next: Color_Grid_Pallet — a colour assigned to an address can become an exception that stays.</footer></main></body></html>'''
(O/'index.html').write_text(page,encoding='utf-8')
diffs=[]
for rel in json.loads((O/'baseline-hashes.json').read_text()):
 if rel.endswith('/final.md'):continue
 diffs.extend(difflib.unified_diff((O/'before'/rel).read_text(encoding='utf-8').splitlines(True),(R/rel).read_text(encoding='utf-8').splitlines(True),fromfile='before/'+rel,tofile=rel))
(O/'source-changes.diff').write_text(''.join(diffs),encoding='utf-8')
print('Built current reading, native comparisons and exact changes.')
